{"name":"Clamshell","hex":"#edd0b6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"clamshell","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The shell of a clam.","Any object that, in (literal or figurative) resemblance to the shell of a clam, has a hinge on one edge and two surfaces that close together.\n\nA dredging bucket with hinges like the shell of a clam.\n\nIn food service, the closing box (usually styrofoam but sometimes cardboard) given to consumers with takeout food.\nA hinged case for a video tape, cassette tape, or video game cartridge.\n  A person's mouth."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To deform a die in a shape resembling the shell of a clam, as a result of uneven extrusion pressure.","To dig out by means of a clamshell (dredging bucket)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clamshell"}],"entries":[{"title":"Scoop stretcher","blocks":[{"text":"The scoop stretcher is a device used specifically for moving injured people. It is ideal for carrying casualties with possible spinal injuries."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Civiere_a_aubes.png/330px-Civiere_a_aubes.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scoop_stretcher"},{"title":"Clamshell design","blocks":[{"text":"Clamshell design is a form factor commonly used in the design of electronic devices and other manufactured objects. It is inspired by the morphology of the clam. The form factor has been applied to handheld game consoles, mobile phones, and especially laptop computers. Clamshell devices are usually made of two sections connected by a hinge, each section containing either a flat panel display or an alphanumeric keyboard/keypad, which can fold into contact together like a bivalve shell."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Clams_on_Sandy_Hook_beaches_-_panoramio.jpg/330px-Clams_on_Sandy_Hook_beaches_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clamshell_design"},{"title":"Clamshell (container)","blocks":[{"text":"A clamshell is a one-piece container consisting of two halves joined by a hinge area which allows the structure to come together to close. Clamshells can be made to be reusable and reclosable, or can be sealed securely, requiring that they be cut open. They are commonly made of thermoformed plastic."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/PET-Verpackung-offen.jpg/330px-PET-Verpackung-offen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clamshell_(container)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Civiere_a_aubes.jpg/500px-Civiere_a_aubes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Civiere_a_aubes.jpg/500px-Civiere_a_aubes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A scoop stretcher. Note that the stretcher is upside down: the narrow end of the stretcher is for the patient's legs and feet.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACiviere_a_aubes.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Clamshell_iBook_G3.jpg/330px-Clamshell_iBook_G3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Clamshell_iBook_G3.jpg/330px-Clamshell_iBook_G3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AClamshell_iBook_G3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/THinkPad345C.jpg/500px-THinkPad345C.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74